{
  "_readme": [
    "BathhouseSim modeling colour source of truth (read by bh_lib.py apply_asset_palette).",
    "themes: zone looks. kinds = material type per role (paint | wood | metal); colors = sRGB hex per role.",
    "assets: which theme each asset uses + per-asset overrides. Override a colour with \"body\": \"#RRGGBB\",",
    "or colour and material with \"body\": {\"kind\": \"wood\", \"color\": \"#RRGGBB\"}. Then re-run run_all.sh for that asset.",
    "Material roles: body (main shell), body_dk (frames, doors, trims), light (tops, caps, panel fields), accent (knobs, needles, levers), hot, cold.",
    "Colour-only roles: tile_a, tile_b, tile_band, tile_grout, label, ink, dial_red, sign_ink, shade, mirror, white.",
    "tier / age: condition. tiers maps an install tier to age (0 = brand new, no chips/rust/dirt at all; 0.7 = worn tier-1 look). Low tiers are worn, higher tiers get progressively cleaner. Per asset: assets.<asset>.tier selects the age; assets.<asset>.age (if set) overrides it."
  ],
